url":"https://api.github.com/users/Veradictus/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Veradictus/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Veradictus/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-22T22:53:08Z","updated_at":"2025-10-22T22:53:41Z","body":"> Tested with the following configuration: `Godot v4.6.dev2 - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - AMD Radeon RX 9070 XT (Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.; 32.0.21025.10016) - AMD Ryzen 9 5950X 16-Core Processor (32 threads) - 31.91 GiB memory` Adrenalin 25.9.1\n> \n> No crashes. I'll quickly install 25.9.2 and re-test.\n> \n> Edit: 25.9.2 also works without issues for me.\n> \n> I'd like to determine if RDNA4 GPUs (\"9000 Series\") just might not have this issue, or if it could be Windows 11 related.\n> \n> [@Veradictus](https://github.com/Veradictus) and [@NuncaGit](https://github.com/NuncaGit) do you run Windows 10 or Windows 11?\n> \n> Edit2: I do have a Win10 and Win11 mini PC somewhere (both with Vega-something iGPUs). Can probably test tomorrow\n\nOS: Windows 11 build 22631.6060\nCPU: AMD Ryzen 9 5950X 16-Core Processor\nRAM: 128GB\nGPU: RX 7900 XTX\nAMD Software Ver: 25.8.1\n\nGodot build is blank pull from the repo w/ double precision enabled.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3434454959/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3434570307","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111879#issuecomment-3434570307","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111879","id":3434570307,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Mt2JD","user":{"login":"Alex2782","id":41921395,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxOTIxMzk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41921395?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782","html_url":"https://github.com/Alex2782","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-22T23:43:23Z","updated_at":"2025-10-22T23:43:23Z","body":"`AMD Software 25.9.1`\n\n`Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - AMD Radeon 780M Graphics (Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.; 32.0.21025.10016) - AMD Ryzen 9 7940HS w/ Radeon 780M Graphics (16 threads) - 47.78 GiB memory`\n\n\nAlso reproducible on my Windows 11 (mini) PC. I couldn't debug it with VS 2022. The AMD tool reports it as a driver timeout. My PC freezes for about five seconds, the monitor briefly goes black, and sometimes my monitor goes into standby mode. I've been observing this behavior for about a month now; it sometimes happens when I start YouTube videos. (Google Chrome)\n\n-------\n\n> Edit: Unable to bisect right now as the driver crash completely slows down my computer, so I would probably have to reboot every time, I'll see tomorrow if it gets easier after rebooting after these crashes\n\n\nI could also try `bisect` when I find the time. After four crashes, I haven't noticed any slowdown. It's just annoying that my monitor goes into standby mode, and I have to try several times until the video signal/input source is correctly recognized.\n\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3434570307/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3435384942","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111879#issuecomment-3435384942","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111879","id":3435384942,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Mw9Bu","user":{"login":"Sch1nken","id":11414422,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNDE0NDIy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11414422?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken","html_url":"https://github.com/Sch1nken","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-23T06:34:58Z","updated_at":"2025-10-23T06:35:09Z","body":"It might be a bit early but it seems all reported crashes happen on Windows 11. Though also only in \"older\" GPUs. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3435384942/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"co